you've probably all heard about medical  racism where people of color get worse  health care because of their race and  that's usually due to human bias so it's  important that doctors rely less on  their feelings and more on the numbers  except did you know that numbers can be  racist too i'll tell you more in a  segment called how did we get here  tonight we're going to talk about  medicine and just a little tip laughter  is not the best one if you don't believe  me find someone with a peanut allergy  give them a rhesus cup and then tell  them a knock knock joke  knock knock they're dead now  specifically we're going to talk about a  practice in medicine called race  correction that's when medical  calculations are adjusted based on a  patient's race and race correction can  result in disastrous outcomes for people  of color now these adjustments affect  just about every part of the body but  since we're still in a giant respiratory  pandemic let's start by talking about  the lungs i think of them as the tia and  tamara of the human body because there  are two of them and they are very close  to my heart  for more than a century doctors have  assumed that black people have a smaller  lung capacity than white people why well  to understand we're going to have to go  all the way back to 1851 to meet a man  named samuel cartwright now i'm going to  warn you you're going to be really mad  at this guy but you can never hate him  as much as his own barber obviously did  now cartwright was a white doctor who  decided he was going to investigate  quote the diseases and physical  peculiarities of the negro race which is  already a red flag right there  it's like when you go on a first date  and the guy tells you all his exes are  crazy  chad  the only thing all those girls have in  common is you  now lo and behold dr cartwright  discovered a bunch of what he called  negro diseases for example he insisted  he found one called drapedomania that  was rampant in the black population he  said that this horrifying disease and i  swear i'm not making it up induces the  negro to run away from service that's  right this white man thought that  enslaved people were running away  because of a medical disease and not and  i'm just spitballing here because  they're enslaved  that's basically like saying i've  discovered a disease that makes a  waitress spit in my food every time i  grab her ass i call it diner mania  also  cartwright discovered another disease  that i'm not even going to try to  pronounce because he made it up so why  should i bother  cartwright claimed that this disease  made enslaved people  lazy  that's right the enslaved people were  lazy not the white people enjoying a  mint julep while they did all the work  and the main symptom of this disease  lesions on the enslaved people's backs  now i wonder how they got there and this  will probably come as no surprise  cartwright said the best treatment for  his made-up disease was more  whipping  that's the worst medical prescription  since well laughter so what does all of  this have to do with the lung capacity  we were talking about earlier okay well  on top of everything else cartwright was  also the first doctor to measure um lung  capacity between black and white people  he called something he used something  called a spirometer which looks like a  very scientific bond  and he concluded that black people have  a lower lung capacity than white people  now my instinct would be not to believe  anything this reverse eddie munster said  but the medical profession went a  different way because to this day  spirometers use a race-based correction  that assumes that a  10 to 15 percent smaller lung capacity  for black patients but the actual  science on that is very unclear race is  connected to things like access to  health care or likelihood of living in  polluted areas things that people of  color are more likely to experience so  while there's no evidence that race  determines lung health there is plenty  of evidence that racism could and those  are the kinds of things an algorithm  does not pick up besides anyone who  wants to say that black people have weak  lungs should be required to listen to  whitney houston do this  [Applause]  she tricked us into loving america yeah  that woman has the lung capacity of 1  000 women and one hot air balloon now  why does all this talk of lung capacity  matter well because if you think someone  has diminished lung capacity then you're  not as worried when they get a  respiratory infection and their numbers  are lower you might take longer to get  the medical care which could lead to  more serious illness and all those small  decisions add up for example according  to the cdc black people are currently  hospitalized for covid at a rate two and  a half times that of white people so the  numbers matter and it's not just the  lungs that are affected by these  algorithms because the racism creeps  through all the rest of the body as well  for example black women have the highest  rates of c-section at least partially  because of something called a v-back  score the v-back score is an algorithm  that estimates the chance a woman has of  a successful vaginal birth after she's  had a c-section think of it like an  s-a-t for your vag  the v-back score is important because  c-sections are much riskier than vaginal  births and up until just a couple months  ago the v-back actually automatically  said that black and latinx women had a  higher risk score than white women that  means more women of color were advised  to get a c-section which can be  dangerous but recently researchers  looked into why that was included in the  algorithm at all and like marjorie  taylor green says to herself every  morning when she looks in the mirror get  ready for some racism  because  they realize the algorithm was based on  an old study that found that being  unmarried and not having insurance  actually increased the risk it wasn't  race at all but someone saw a single  parent and lack of health care access  and program that into their little  algorithm as black and latinx which is  so devastatingly racist i'd like to find  whoever wrote it and give them this  haircut  but  guess what it gets worse because the  american heart association has something  called a heart failure risk score that's  the score doctors use to predict the  risk of death in patients who have been  admitted to the hospital the higher the  score the greater your risk it's a  single number that can change your life  think of it like the powerball except  the prize is getting admitted to the  hospital  according to the new england journal of  medicine the heart failure risk score  automatically assigns three additional  points to any patient identified as  non-black  so basically think of those points like  jokes on an episode of prairie home  companion you're gonna get a whole lot  more of them if you're white  now what this means for parents is that  the algorithm automatically categorizes  all black patients as lower risk whether  they are or not and that has dangerous  results a 2019 study found that black  and latinx patients with heart failure  were less likely than white patients to  be admitted to the cardiology service  that's heartbreaking literally and the  list goes on a race-adjusted algorithm  makes black americans kidney function  look better even though they have higher  rates of end-stage kidney disease a  different algorithm used by hospitals to  decide which patients get follow-up care  let healthier white patients into the  programs ahead of black patients who  were sicker and the examples are endless  but my point is hospitals treat people  not numbers patients of color deserve to  go to the doctor and receive health care  without bias and for doctors to take  into account their individual  circumstances instead of their race  but until then every single person who  makes one of these racist algorithms  should have to get the cart right this  has been how did we get here  [Applause]  [Music]  so  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

